  "overview": {
    "asOf": "2026-10-14",
    "items": [
      {
        "text": "Derek Tran is the U.S. Representative for California’s 45th District, serving since 2025. He sits on the House Armed Services and Small Business committees, where he is the ranking member of the Oversight, Investigations, and Regulations subcommittee. He served in the Army Reserve, worked as an attorney for consumers and workers, and co-owns a pharmacy. He served on the Consumer Attorneys Association of Los Angeles and California board and as an Orange traffic commissioner.",
        "cites": [1, 2],
        "sentences": [
          {
            "text": "Derek Tran is the U.S. Representative for California’s 45th District, serving since 2025.",
            "cites": [1]
          },
          {
            "text": "He sits on the House Armed Services and Small Business committees, where he is the ranking member of the Oversight, Investigations, and Regulations subcommittee.",
            "cites": [1]
          },
          {
            "text": "He served in the Army Reserve, worked as an attorney for consumers and workers, and co-owns a pharmacy.",
            "cites": [2]
          },
          {
            "text": "He served on the Consumer Attorneys Association of Los Angeles and California board and as an Orange traffic commissioner.",
            "cites": [2]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Tran says the rising cost of gas, groceries, and rent is the most important issue, and Congress must expand affordable healthcare, protect food stamps, and end costly tariffs. He says he co-founded the Lowering Costs Caucus and urged the Trump administration to address rising prices. He says he secured $250,000 for affordable housing and backed the 21st Century ROAD to Housing Act. In 2025, he voted for the Laken Riley Act to detain undocumented immigrants accused of theft-related crimes. In 2026, he voted against resolutions disapproving of California’s EPA pollution waivers for nonroad engines and harbor craft.",
        "cites": [3, 1, 4],
        "sentences": [
          {
            "text": "Tran says the rising cost of gas, groceries, and rent is the most important issue, and Congress must expand affordable healthcare, protect food stamps, and end costly tariffs.",
            "cites": [3]
          },
          {
            "text": "He says he co-founded the Lowering Costs Caucus and urged the Trump administration to address rising prices.",
            "cites": [3]
          },
          {
            "text": "He says he secured $250,000 for affordable housing and backed the 21st Century ROAD to Housing Act.",
            "cites": [3]
          },
          {
            "text": "In 2025, he voted for the Laken Riley Act to detain undocumented immigrants accused of theft-related crimes.",
            "cites": [1]
          },
          {
            "text": "In 2026, he voted against resolutions disapproving of California’s EPA pollution waivers for nonroad engines and harbor craft.",
            "cites": [4]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "In 2026, he sponsored the Housing COST Act. He helped introduce the No Getting Rich in Congress Act to prohibit members from buying and selling individual stocks. He cosponsored the COPS Reauthorization Act to fund hiring, training, and equipment for local law enforcement. His 504 Program Risk Oversight Act requiring annual risk analyses of SBA loans advanced in committee in 2025. His office says he secured over $14 million for public safety, health, infrastructure, and housing.",
        "cites": [5, 1, 6, 7, 8],
        "sentences": [
          {
            "text": "In 2026, he sponsored the Housing COST Act.",
            "cites": [5]
          },
          {
